questions.answer:
Any two of:
- filtering the blood to remove nitrogenous wastes such as **urea** (excretion);
- regulating water balance (osmoregulation) and salt/electrolyte balance;
- regulating blood pH;
- regulating blood pressure.

A **line graph** (both variables are continuous):
- $x$-axis (independent variable): "Number of wraps in myelin sheath", even scale 0–5;
- $y$-axis (dependent variable): "Conduction velocity (m s$^{-1}$)", even scale 0–2.0;
- all five points plotted accurately as crosses;
- a smooth **curve of best fit** through the points that does not extend beyond the data (not started at the origin) and has no arrowheads;
- a title, e.g. "Effect of myelin sheath thickness on conduction velocity".

A line graph (or column graph) with:
- $x$-axis: "Year of diagnosis" (2011–2015);
- $y$-axis: "Number of new cases of mesothelioma", with an even scale (e.g. 0–700);
- two lines/series, one for males and one for females, with all points plotted accurately;
- a key identifying males and females, and a title.

A line graph with:
- **independent variable on the $x$-axis:** "Duration of diabetes (years)", with an even scale from 0 to 35;
- **dependent variable on the $y$-axis:** "Percentage of participants with glaucoma (%)", with an even scale from 0 to 14;
- all eight points plotted accurately (as crosses);
- a single smooth curve (or line) of best fit — not dot-to-dot;
- a title, e.g. "Percentage of diabetic participants with glaucoma vs duration of diabetes".

